# Tracer: numeric predicate domains reuse checked argument WD.
# Former rejected MIL goal (before proof-body execution):
# ? forall X finite_set, A, B power_set(X):
#     $is_finite_set(A)
#     $is_finite_set(B)
#     $is_nonempty_set(B)
#     B $subset A
#     =>:
#         finite_set_size(set_minus(A, B)) < finite_set_size(A)
# Before: the comparison goal rechecked the finite-difference cardinality
# under a lower ceiling and failed its real-membership domain before the body.
# The active proof supplies the cardinality's natural type; no trust is used.
# Boundary: missing finiteness and undefined division still fail argument WD.
# Run: target/release/litex -strict -lang en -f examples/wd/checked_argument_numeric_domain.lit
thm finite_difference_cardinality_is_nonnegative:
    ? forall A finite_set, B set:
        finite_set_size(set_minus(A, B)) >= 0
    finite_set_size(set_minus(A, B)) $in N
